# Chat scroll performance (macOS)

Random trackpad choke while scrolling a live agent turn is almost always UI-isolate work under the fling — not “scroll physics.” Preserve these invariants; do not “simplify” them away.

## Do not

- Rebuild the transcript `ListView` mid-gesture (`_transcriptUiEpoch`, `setState` on the chat shell, freeze capture).
- Call `_onUserScrollEnded` / clear `_userScrollGesture` on `UserScrollNotification.idle` — on macOS that fires when the finger lifts while **ballistic inertia still runs**. Only `ScrollEndNotification` means settled.
- Bump `_chromeUiEpoch` (or any notifier) during `_userScrollGesture`. Stay dirty; flush after scroll end.
- Parse `GptMarkdown` for rows that newly enter the viewport while scrolling.
- Fight the trackpad with `jumpTo` / refollow while `_userScrollGesture` or `!_followOutput`.
- Re-introduce tool-card shimmer / live tickers during unfollow or mid-fling (`animate: _followOutput`, `TickerMode` via `_transcriptMotionN`).

## Do keep

- **`TranscriptScrollBusy` + `MessageBody`**: while busy, first-time markdown is plain `Text`; already-frozen bubbles must **not** `dependOn` the scope (avoids list-wide rebuild). Upgrade markdown after settle, budgeted (~2/frame).
- **PDF / unfollow**: defer `_frozenTranscript` capture until scroll end (`_freezeCapturePending`); while unfollowed, flushes refresh chrome only.
- **Split epochs**: `_transcriptUiEpoch` (list) vs `_chromeUiEpoch` (status/activity). Streaming must not rebuild the list every ACP tick.
- **ADSM `_drainStdout`**: yield often (heavy lines / every few lines) so NDJSON parse cannot starve frames.
- Tool payloads stay out of the list until expand; collapse drops them.

## If scroll chokes again

Check in order: (1) mid-fling transcript/chrome notifier bumps, (2) markdown build on item insert, (3) ADSM/tool upsert work on the UI isolate, (4) `jumpTo` while following.
